  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "The hotel brands most commonly considered for **branded residences** in the **Caribbean and Latin America** include **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, Ritz-Carlton Reserve, Mandarin Oriental, Hyatt’s Andaz, Six Senses, Aman, Hilton, Kimpton, and Marriott’s Luxury Collection / Residences portfolio**.[1][3][4][5][6][7][9]\n\nIn the Caribbean specifically, the most visible and frequently cited names are **Four Seasons**, **Ritz-Carlton**, **Mandarin Oriental**, **Andaz**, **Six Senses**, and **Aman**.[1][3][4][6][7][8] Hyatt and Hilton are also active in the region, and Marriott-branded projects show up through **Ritz-Carlton**, **The Luxury Collection**, **Kimpton**, and broader **Residences by Marriott** offerings.[3][5][6][7][9]\n\nA practical way to think about the market is:\n\n- **Ultra-luxury global flags:** Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve, Mandarin Oriental, Aman, Six Senses[1][4][6][7][8]\n- **Lifestyle / resort brands:** Andaz, Kimpton, SLS, Nikki Beach, Anantara[1][4][6][8]\n- **Broader hospitality groups with branded-home platforms:** Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt[3][5][6][9]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **top brands by prestige**, **by current Caribbean presence**, or **by Latin America projects outside the Caribbean**.",
